sigill: the re-trap guard counts the same frame, not the same PC

bionic_shim.cpp (macapk_sigill_handler). The handler chains a SIGILL it does
not emulate to HotSpot, and guards against a chained handler that returns
without advancing: three traps in a row at one PC on one thread restore SIG_DFL
and re-raise. But HotSpot's NativeDeoptInstruction (0xd4ade001) sits at a return
site inside the method being deoptimized, and every activation of that method
still on the thread's stack returns through it. A recursive method therefore
traps at one PC once per nested activation -- each serviced, each at its own SP
-- and the third one was taken for a loop and killed the process.

The guard now requires the same PC and the same SP. A handler that silently
returns re-traps with every register unchanged, so the real loop is still caught.

Measured on Instagram 455: "chain looping on same PC; restoring default and
re-raising" with insn 0xd4ade001 killed 2 of 10 launches 7-8s after the first
frame (while the feed and inbox rows were being inflated), and showed up at
shutdown in 1-2 logs of every earlier 10-launch run. After: see the table in
contrib/upstream/README.md.

diff --git a/runtime/translator/src/bionic_shim.cpp b/runtime/translator/src/bionic_shim.cpp
--- a/runtime/translator/src/bionic_shim.cpp
+++ b/runtime/translator/src/bionic_shim.cpp
@@ -14100,13 +14187,28 @@ chain:
         // starts at 1 on a fresh PC; >= kMaxSamePcTraps means we have
         // already chained (kMaxSamePcTraps-1) times on this exact PC
         // without it advancing -> treat as a silent-return loop.
+        //
+        // "The same site" is the same PC in the same FRAME (same SP). A deopt
+        // trap sits at a return site inside the method being deoptimized, and
+        // EVERY activation of that method still on this thread's stack returns
+        // through it: a recursive method traps at one PC once per nested
+        // activation, each of them serviced and each at its own SP. Counting
+        // the PC alone called the third of those a loop and killed the process
+        // (Instagram 455: "chain looping on same PC" with insn 0xd4ade001, in
+        // 2 of 10 launches 7-8s after the first frame, while the recursive
+        // layout inflation of the feed and inbox rows was running; before
+        // that, on 1-2 of every 10 shutdowns). A handler that silently returns
+        // re-traps with every register unchanged, SP included.
         constexpr unsigned kMaxSamePcTraps = 3;
         static thread_local uintptr_t t_ill_last_pc = 0;
+        static thread_local uintptr_t t_ill_last_sp = 0;
         static thread_local unsigned  t_ill_same_count = 0;
-        if (pc_log != 0 && pc_log == t_ill_last_pc) {
+        const uintptr_t sp_log = uc->uc_mcontext ? uc->uc_mcontext->__ss.__sp : 0;
+        if (pc_log != 0 && pc_log == t_ill_last_pc && sp_log == t_ill_last_sp) {
             ++t_ill_same_count;
         } else {
             t_ill_last_pc = pc_log;
+            t_ill_last_sp = sp_log;
             t_ill_same_count = 1;
         }
         const bool looping = (t_ill_same_count >= kMaxSamePcTraps);
